# Ant Design — Next.js App Router

## Do not use dot notation for subcomponents

Next.js App Router **cannot serialize** antd compound subcomponents accessed via dot notation when they cross the server/client boundary.

```tsx
// BAD — breaks in Server Components or when imported from server parents
<Form.Item>...</Form.Item>
<Typography.Title>...</Typography.Title>
<Input.Password />
<Select.Option />
<Menu.Item />
```

Error you may see:

```text
Cannot access .Item on the server. You cannot dot into a client module from a server component.
```

Top-level antd imports (`Button`, `Card`, `Table`) are fine. The issue is **static subcomponents on client modules**.

## Required pattern

Import subcomponents from `@/components/ui/antd` (project wrappers) or directly from antd paths:

```tsx
import { Form, FormItem } from "@/components/ui/antd";
import { Title, Paragraph } from "@/components/ui/antd";
import { Input, PasswordInput } from "@/components/ui/antd";

<Form>
  <FormItem label="نام کاربری">
    <Input />
  </FormItem>
</Form>
```

## When `'use client'` is not enough

Marking a page `'use client'` avoids the error but forfeits SSR for that page. Prefer named subcomponent imports so pages and layouts can stay Server Components where possible.

## Adding new subcomponents

When you need another dotted API (e.g. `Select.Option`, `Tabs.TabPane`, `Layout.Content`, `Layout.Sider`):

1. Add a `'use client'` re-export in `src/components/ui/antd/`.
2. Export a named component (e.g. `SelectOption`, `LayoutContent`).
3. Never use dot notation in JSX.

